Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:13:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/19] Measure seed staleness and widen the seed-source
 options

Estimating month t from the supply observed in month t-k doubles the share
error at one month of lag (1.96 -> 4.04 pp) and the fit refuses to run in 8
of 11 months, because a median of 25 competitive routes per month did not
exist the month before.  The seed is a subscription, not a purchase.

Split the source table into published schedules and tracked flights, since
they fail for different reasons: schedules do not depend on ADS-B receiver
density, and cancellations are row scaling that the fit cancels.  Record that
the AICM bulletin and the DATATUR base were opened and carry no carrier-by-
route breakdown.

Add the acceptance test that would have ruled out OpenSky in one afternoon:
compare a trial month against the flights-per-route AFAC already publishes,
and look for coverage that differs between carriers within a route.

